<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak c.bank reserves dip to $3.457 bln - March 5.</title>
<headline>Slovak c.bank reserves dip to $3.457 bln - March 5.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) on Friday said its hard currency reserves dipped to $3.457 billion as of March 5, from $3.514 billion on February 26.</p>
<p>HARD CURRENCY RESERVES  March 5  Feb 26  Jan 29  Dec 31/96</p>
<p>  NBS reserves ($bln)    3.457    3.514   3.418    3.473</p>
<p>  Commercial banks	 1.831    1.830   1.920    2.321</p>
<p>  Entire banking sector  5.288    5.344   5.338    5.794</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521-8402</p>
</text>
